Line 4: "loan * r / (1 - (1 + r) to the power of -n) rounded to 2 decimal places" could mean two things.
    let payment be loan * r / (1 - (1 + r) to the power of -n) rounded to 2 decimal places.
                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
To round the whole value, write "loan * r / (1 - (1 + r) to the power of -n), rounded to 2 decimal places". To round only the last part, write "loan * r / ((1 - (1 + r) to the power of -n) rounded to 2 decimal places)".

Line 5: "4.8 / 20 rounded to 2 decimal places" could mean two things.
    let density be 4.8 / 20 rounded to 2 decimal places.
                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
To round the whole value, write "4.8 / 20, rounded to 2 decimal places". To round only the last part, write "4.8 / (20 rounded to 2 decimal places)".

Line 6: "3 plus 2.5 rounded" could mean two things.
    let x be 3 plus 2.5 rounded.
             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
To round the whole value, write "3 plus 2.5, rounded". To round only the last part, write "3 plus (2.5 rounded)".
